5. Unicode / Unihan
================================================================================

  Status        NOT bundled in v0.1.

  The v0.1 canon derives simplified/traditional pairing and pinyin from
  CC-CEDICT and the pinned HSK list, not from the Unicode Han Database. If a
  later release adds radical decomposition, variant mappings, or stroke data
  sourced from Unihan, this section becomes live and the following applies:

    Source      Unicode Han Database (Unihan), Unicode Character Database
    Home        https://www.unicode.org/charts/unihan.html
    Licence     Unicode License v3
                https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

  The Unicode License requires the copyright notice and permission notice to
  accompany the data. Do not add Unihan-derived fields without adding that
  notice here in the same commit.

================================================================================
6. Audio
================================================================================

  Status        NOT published in v0.1. Every audio field in every record
                reports status "pending" and emits no URL.

  When audio ships it is SayMei-generated (ElevenLabs synthesis in two named
  voices, plus lines extracted from SayMei's own dialogue masters), served by
  URL from a SayMei host, and never bundled into the dataset. It is not
  covered by data/LICENSE; its terms will be published alongside it. Nothing
  in this repository grants rights to audio that does not yet exist.

